{"id": "EUVD-2026-80440", "enisaUuid": "c64f836b-7f1c-3b78-9971-9cb2787fd3c1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nf2fs: validate MOVE_RANGE destination size\n\nF2FS_IOC_MOVE_RANGE checks the source range, but not the destination end\nbefore updating i_size. A source hole can expose this: __clone_blkaddrs()\nskips NULL_ADDR entries and returns success, so the caller can still extend\nthe destination inode with unchecked pos_out + len.\n\nReject destination overflow and use inode_newsize_ok() before extending\nthe destination inode.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:49:02", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/54c587f3f95ce2d6932a16566db83f73cc4313e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bca61ee5192ea47003722486ae9588a2a4bb47b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db13064669526494cd78ba3a4394063b740e940c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dcae1eeda53149f219dd6af93b3083b7271c1c63", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e533889fc26aea0cd83c90327063f272061dd820"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6fmr-6rhp-m3p8", "CVE-2026-89840"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09834f84-0498-382a-a59f-8230c0da2218", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1ec1533d-8e3c-355c-a2c1-dc1c36744e7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4dd6f977fc778e5a0da604e5f8cb2f36d163d27b <e533889fc26aea0cd83c90327063f272061dd820"}, {"id": "3ca025a1-4642-3c9b-a9d2-16283b9781c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.8"}, {"id": "3e64033e-37a1-388e-af70-aefb0d19929a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "442c0387-8701-3948-8ce9-e1b211cb7aa0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": 